course: dictionary
lesson: 12445
title: Decrease: getting smaller
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To decrease is to become smaller, fewer or less. «The water level decreased after the hot summer.» The water got lower, so decreased means went down.
explain: You can also decrease something on purpose, like turning the volume down. «She decreased the speed of her bike before the corner.» She made the speed smaller.
explain: A decrease can also be a noun, meaning the fall itself. «There was a sharp decrease in rain this month.» Sharp shows the fall was big and quick. To check, swap in the word fall or drop and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Decrease is a verb and a noun: you decrease something, or you notice a decrease.
fact: The opposite of decrease is increase, which means to become bigger or more.
fact: In maths, «decrease 50 by 10» means take away 10 from 50, so the answer is 40.
fact: 10% of 50 is 5, so a 10% decrease of 50 takes away 5.
fact: On a graph, a decrease shows as a line going down as you move to the right.
exercise: «The population of the village decreased over ten years.» What does decreased mean? | Moved to a new village | Stayed exactly the same | *Became smaller in number | Became bigger in number
exercise: What is 50 decreased by 10? | 60 | 500 | 5 | *40
exercise: Which word means the opposite of decrease? | *increase | drop | stay | pause
test: «The price of apples decreased after the summer harvest.» What happened to the price? | *It went down | It stayed the same | It disappeared | It went up
test: «There was a sharp decrease in the number of birds in the park.» What does sharp suggest? | *A quick, big fall | A change in colour | A slow, gentle change | A sudden rise
exam: On a graph, what does a decrease look like? | A flat line | *A line going down | A line going up | A circle
